    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi></math> be the median of the triangle with vertices <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. The equation of the line passing through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></math>and parallel to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi></math> is&nbsp;"
